![Moodbit](moodbit.png)

I was a *remote* contractor for the _Moodbit_ company (New York,
USA) during some months of 2018 and 2019. My work consisted of
developing a chatbot for _Slack_ that used machine learning
algorithms to evaluate people's "feelings" and "emotions" in the
chat. I also built a _Dashboard_ that integrated with _AWS
Quicksight_ to show the results.

## Technologies Used

- AWS Lambda (Javascript and Python).
- AWS Sagemaker (Python).
- AWS RDS (Database).
- AWS API Gateway (Endpoints).
- AWS Cognito (User Accounts).
- AWS Quicksight (Information Panels and Reports).
- Slack SDK (Slack Connection).
- Google Cloud Natural Language (Text Sentiment Analysis).
- React.js (Frontend).
- Firebase (Hosting).

## Tasks

- Program _AWS Lambda_ functions for _Slack_ integration.
- Database design in _AWS RDS_.
- Create a dashboard in _AWS Quicksight_.
- Create a frontend with _React.js_ to integrate _AWS Cognito_ and
  _AWS Quicksight_.
- Configure _AWS SageMaker_ to integrate with _AWS Lambda_ and
  deliver results.
- Integrate with the _Google CNL_ API.
- Configure _Firebase_ to host the website.

## Challenge

Additionally I prepared a code _Challenge_ to evaluate candidates
joining the team.

- [Moodbit Challenge](challenge.pdf)

